sequenceDiagram
    participant Proc as Process
    participant Kernel
    participant Handler as Signal Handler
    
    Proc->>Kernel: sigaction(SIGINT, &act, NULL)
    Note over Kernel: Register handler
    
    Proc->>Proc: Normal execution
    
    Note over Kernel: User presses Ctrl+C
    Kernel->>Kernel: Generate SIGINT
    Kernel->>Proc: Deliver signal (interrupt execution)
    
    Note over Proc: Save context
    Proc->>Handler: Call handler function
    Handler->>Handler: signal_handler(int sig)
    Handler->>Handler: Set flag / cleanup
    Handler-->>Proc: Return
    Note over Proc: Restore context
    
    Proc->>Proc: Check flag in main loop
    Proc->>Proc: if (quit_flag) cleanup & exit
    
    rect rgb(255, 240, 240)
        Note over Proc,Handler: Async-signal-safe functions only:, write(), _exit(), sigprocmask()
    end
    
    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
        Note over Proc,Handler: NOT safe: printf, malloc, etc.
    end
